anks for catching this.</p>\n<p>Yes you are right.</p>\n<p>That’s the only way the formula type-checks, but it is also confirmed by the formula below (3.1.6) in <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/IPC-property#KashiwaraSchapira2006\">Kashiwara &amp; Schapira 2006 p. 84-85</a>, where this statement is taken from.</p>\n<p>I have fixed it. Also made some editorial adjustments to this old entry.</p>\n<p>Any further discussion is best moved to the entry’s discussion thread <a href=\"#narrow/channel/2/topic/IPC-property/near/123480\">here</a>.</p>","timestamp":1768840457,"subject":"IPC-property canonical morphism","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]}]